+Recent visual generators study mixture assignment and the geometry of
+distribution matching\cite{mgflow,semot}. These results motivate more expressive
+writing distributions, but marginal image fidelity cannot certify an answer.
+A generator that swaps the correct images for two equally frequent questions
+preserves the answer-image distribution while answering both incorrectly.
+Conditional supervision and prompt interventions therefore remain necessary;
+natural-image gains do not establish a shortcut to language learning.
+
